The lemma is false as stated, even when the bond attains the optimized \(M\).

I constructed a family with fixed \(d=8\), \(M=3/2\), and infrared \(A=1\), but
\[
\liminf_{\text{smooth limit}}
\frac{\operatorname{Def}(w)}{M\sum_x(\Delta w_x)^2/w_x}
\ge \frac{1}{300\delta}.
\]
Here \(2\delta>0\) is a spectator gap that can be arbitrarily small. For quadratic modular weights, the spectator contributes \((100\delta)^{-1}\log L+O_\delta(1)\), so the obstruction survives at logarithmic order. This does not disprove the velocity-weighted bound.

